From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 01:54:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: inter-RAT downgrade detector (T-OR-057)

RatDowngradeAnalyzer (default off) flags a network-directed move off LTE
toward a legacy/sunset RAT, complementing the broadcast-reselection
analyzers (priority_2g_downgrade for SIB6/7, connection_redirect_downgrade
for a Connection Release redirect).

A MobilityFromEUTRACommand is classified by purpose and, for a Handover, by
the decoded target RAT:
- CellChangeOrder (always GERAN) or a Handover to GERAN -> High (a directed
  2G downgrade).
- A Handover or e-CSFB to 3G/UTRA or CDMA2000 -> Informational.
- A Handover to NR (5G) or E-UTRA -> ignored (not a downgrade).
The event message notes when cs-FallbackIndicator is set (usually a
legitimate voice-call fallback), to aid calibration.

An LTE cell broadcasting CDMA2000 interworking (SIB8) -> Low (anomalous
where CDMA2000 is decommissioned; a per-MCC sunset policy to raise it is
T-OR-115). SIB8 repeats on BCCH, so expect a Low event per repetition.

Stateless; keys on the message/IE alone. Off by default pending per-market
calibration. Test vectors are TS 36.331 PDUs encoded with the reference
Python pycrate and decoded here through telcom_parser (two independent
ASN.1 implementations): CellChangeOrder (r8/r9) and Handover to
GERAN/UTRA/CDMA2000/NR, e-CSFB, a CS-fallback-marked handover, SIB8, a real
SystemInformation without SIB8, a SIB1, and a benign reconfiguration.

